IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `nzs-types`

-- New Zealand Superannuation and Retirement Income Act 2001 — GOAL 3: THE
-- RATES AND THE FUND.
--
--   "Are the year's rates within the bounds s 16 sets; what is the required
--    capital contribution to the Fund; may capital be withdrawn; and when is
--    the next performance review due?"
--
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/act_public_2001_84.txt — ss 15-16,
-- 42-47, 71.

§ `Goal 3 — the rates and the Fund`

-- s 16 "(a) the standard weekly amount ... (after the deduction of standard
-- tax) payable to a couple ... is not less than 66% or more than 72.5% of the
-- average ordinary time weekly earnings ... (after the deduction of standard
-- tax and the earner levies ...): (b) ... a single person who is living alone
-- is 65% of the weekly amount ... payable to a couple ...: (c) ... a single
-- person who is not living alone is 60%". All amounts after tax.
@ref s 16
@export Whether a year's after-tax rates of New Zealand superannuation meet s 16 of the New Zealand Superannuation and Retirement Income Act 2001: the couple's combined amount between 66% and 72.5% of the after-tax average ordinary time weekly earnings, the single living alone amount 65% of the couple amount, and the single sharing amount 60%. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN couple IS A NUMBER  @desc The weekly amount, after standard tax, for a couple both qualified
      alone IS A NUMBER  @desc The weekly amount, after standard tax, for a single person living alone
      sharing IS A NUMBER  @desc The weekly amount, after standard tax, for a single person not living alone
      wage IS A NUMBER  @desc The average ordinary time weekly earnings after standard tax and earner levies
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the rates meet s 16, couple` couple `, living alone` alone `, sharing` sharing `, net average wage` wage IF
        couple AT LEAST wage TIMES 66 DIVIDED BY 100
    AND couple AT MOST wage TIMES 72.5 DIVIDED BY 100
    AND alone EQUALS couple TIMES 65 DIVIDED BY 100
    AND sharing EQUALS couple TIMES 60 DIVIDED BY 100

-- s 43 the required annual capital contribution — formula symbols lost; read
-- as the contribution percentage × projected GDP − the expected net cost of
-- New Zealand superannuation for the year (BRIEF.md).
@ref s 43
GIVEN percentage IS A NUMBER, gdp IS A NUMBER, cost IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the required annual capital contribution, percentage` percentage `, GDP` gdp `, net cost` cost MEANS
    (gdp TIMES percentage DIVIDED BY 100) MINUS cost

-- s 47 "(1) If the required annual capital contribution is less than zero,
-- the Minister may require a capital withdrawal to be made from the Fund up
-- to that amount ... (2) However, no capital withdrawal is allowed from the
-- Fund in any financial year commencing before 1 July 2020."
@ref s 47
GIVEN contribution IS A NUMBER, `year starts` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most that may be withdrawn from the Fund, required contribution` contribution `, financial year starting` `year starts` MEANS
    IF   contribution LESS THAN 0 AND `year starts` AT LEAST Date 1 7 2020
    THEN 0 MINUS contribution
    ELSE 0

-- s 44(2) "The requirements of this section do not apply if the required
-- annual capital contribution is less than zero."
@ref s 44
GIVEN required IS A NUMBER, paid IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister must explain a lesser contribution, required` required `, to be paid` paid IF
    required AT LEAST 0 AND paid LESS THAN required

-- s 71(3) "Subsequent performance reviews must be conducted at intervals that
-- are no more than 5 years apart".
@ref s 71(3)
GIVEN last IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the latest the next performance review may be, last review` last MEANS
    `add years` last 5
